# Pearl Product Stress Standard

Canonical detail: `docs/pearl-stress-standard.md`. Coverage ledger: `docs/pearl-stress-coverage.md`. Harness: `npm run stress:pearl` → `scripts/pearl-core-stress.mjs`.

Whenever you audit, stress, review, or claim completion for **any** new or existing feature/flow:

1. Run (or extend) the headed Pearl stress harness against this standard — not unit tests alone.
2. Evaluate from a **first-time / clueless user** with **zero demand**: no required modes, tours, or jargon.
3. Cover all lenses in the standard doc: aesthetics (Read real PNGs), usability, functionality (real effects + hit-test), persistence, companion/director honesty, communication, vision alignment, accessibility, error/empty/recovery, performance feel, trust, cross-surface, naming consistency, undo/confirm.
4. Prefer fixing broken claimed paths over documenting them as acceptable.
5. Never claim production-ready / perfect / fully working / state of the art unless evidence supports that exact claim. State credential, mic, extension, and auth gaps explicitly.

Hard fails: navigation traps, inaccessible primary action, fake Done, silent data loss/dupes, companion fake success, white-dot Pearl fallback, user-facing "orb", gauntlet >5, Studio not M→F→L when structure exists.

## Harness integrity (no false green)

Do **not** treat a check as Companion-UX proof if it:

- Calls `__lensOrbRuntime.run` / `.execute` or seeds `localStorage` instead of Talk→type→**GO hit-test**
- Asserts chat text only without a **named pearl artifact** (stable id + title matching intent)
- Falls back to `pearls[0]` when the intent title is missing
- Accepts `Untitled` / `Orb` / `untitled orb` titles or visible labels after create
- Marks merge/edit/experiment stressed when only privileged runtime verbs on seeded IDs ran
- Uses seed-on-failure, `force: true`, or mocked model success to flip the create/workflow check green

Minimum valid create path: GO hit-test → user echo → status → companion reply → Reef/storage pearl with human title → reload persistence. See `docs/pearl-stress-standard.md` § Harness Integrity.
